Falsifies `system_tests::user::job_undertaker_tests::job_undertaker_says_which_job_it_reaped_and_only_then_is_its_window_free`.

The defect: `job_undertaker` forgets the label the kernel handed it beside the death and
announces every reap as label 0, "unlabeled". It still collects first and still sends on its
badged copy of the spawn endpoint, so the message arrives, with the right badge and the right
tid. A progenitor reading it would free nobody's window: every directory-granted job's window
would stay held, and the pool would refuse its seventh spawn for the life of the boot.

Expected to fail: the `(label, tid)` assertion, "the reaped message named the wrong job".

The hunk's context cites milestone 235 (a command that faults hangs the prompt) and §26 (the fault
endpoint: thread death becomes a message a supervisor holds).

